cff-version: 1.2.0
title: PythonPDDL
message: >-
  If you use PythonPDDL (the jupyddl package) in your work, please cite the
  publication below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lejeune
    given-names: Erwin
repository-code: "https://github.com/openplan-labs/PythonPDDL"
url: "https://openplan-labs.github.io/PythonPDDL/"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free, pure-Python PDDL planning framework: a parser and
  grounder, classical through to state-of-the-art planners, heuristics, and a
  benchmarking harness. Distributed on PyPI as jupyddl.
license: Apache-2.0
version: 2.4.0
keywords:
  - PDDL
  - automated planning
  - heuristic search
  - artificial intelligence
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Jupyddl, an extensible python library for PDDL planning and parsing"
  authors:
    - family-names: Lejeune
      given-names: Erwin
  year: 2021
  doi: 10.13140/RG.2.2.22418.89282
  url: "https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.22418.89282"
